        "A fixed-area exceptional set for positive squared-pole sums \u2014 Alec Kriebel, v1.0.0 (2026-10-17). Problem2307037 / AMR-022-7037, Baernstein, Hayman\u2013Lingham Problem7.37. Full affirmative deduction: every finite positive normalized sum of squared complex poles, arbitrary/repeated locations, has ONE compact exceptional set of exact area pi, independent of R, such that ordinary integral outside it over D_R is at most2*pi*log(R)+pi*(log(2)+1/e) for ALL real R>1. Leading2*pi sharp; additive constant not claimed optimal. Four-page note credits established EH1995 indicator inequality and LP2009 quadrature/smash-sum inputs plus antecedents; related Lin/Guerra work credited. No first-priority/global-openness certification. Leung AMS Abstracts11(1990)p181 and13(1992)p440 mathematical texts inaccessible; relevance unresolved. Other full/final access gaps documented. Three mathematical families, extensive bounded priority audit, portable offline/source-optional diagnostics. Extensive AI assistance; unrefereed, no external human peer review/formal certification. Two successive fresh whole-package reviews passed identical release. https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/1136 Published record: https://zenodo.org/records/23443039"
